AutoName: Context
Summary: Capture your day minute by minute alongside your calendars
Description: |-
  Record activities, thoughts, and decisions in a minute-by-minute ledger. Use
  custom activity categories and review time totals by day, week, month, or year.

  Connect calendars available through Android and choose which confirmed
  activities to synchronize. Calendar and storage permissions are optional.
  Private ledger synchronization is available through a user-selected HTTPS
  WebDAV folder. Optional Microsoft calendar and OneDrive support requires the
  publisher's configured Microsoft app registration and uses proprietary services.

  This edition omits Google's native sign-in SDK and the Expo development client.
  It does not provide direct Google account sign-in. Android calendar access can
  include calendars that another installed application makes available to Android.

RepoType: git
Repo: OWNER_PUBLIC_SOURCE_REPOSITORY_URL

Builds:
  - versionName: 0.1.0
    versionCode: 1
    disable: Public source URL, release commit, pinned build-server toolchain, dependency scan, and native verification are pending
    commit: OWNER_IMMUTABLE_RELEASE_COMMIT
    subdir: apps/mobile
    init:
      - EXPO_PUBLIC_CONTEXT_DISTRIBUTION=fdroid CONTEXT_FDROID_SOURCE_BUILD=1 node scripts/prepare-fdroid.cjs --apply
      - corepack pnpm install --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts
      - EXPO_PUBLIC_CONTEXT_DISTRIBUTION=fdroid corepack pnpm exec expo prebuild --platform android --no-install
      - EXPO_PUBLIC_CONTEXT_DISTRIBUTION=fdroid node scripts/prepare-fdroid.cjs --unsigned-android
    build:
      - cd android && EXPO_PUBLIC_CONTEXT_DISTRIBUTION=fdroid ./gradlew --no-daemon assembleRelease
    output: android/app/build/outputs/apk/release/app-release-unsigned.apk

MaintainerNotes: |-
  The upstream fastlane listing is at repository-root fastlane/metadata/android/en-US.
  This is an unverified source-build candidate, not a completed native build recipe.
  Node 24.19.0 and pnpm 11.25.0 are the upstream development versions. The clean
  F-Droid Linux environment still needs a verified Node/pnpm provision mechanism
  and pinned Android SDK/NDK/JDK configuration. Do not silently depend on tools
  already installed on the developer's workstation.
  Dependency pruning runs before installation and leaves unreachable packages in
  the source lock graph. Check the installed native graph and scanner findings;
  no blanket scanignore or scandelete bypass is supplied.
  Native phone validation, public maintenance history or an applicable inclusion
  exception, and release-tag verification are pending. No screenshots are supplied
  until genuine captures of the native app are available.

